            <title>0.7</title>
            <pubDate>Sat, 07 Nov 2026 17:55:16 -0500</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>60</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.7</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description><![CDATA[<h2>Assembly 0.7</h2>
<p><b>Assembly now uses projects.</b> The first time you open this version, it
asks to move your deep scan into a project. Nothing is scanned again, and your
sound rolls aren't touched.</p>
<p>Why it has to move:</p>
<ul>
  <li><b>Each show remembers its own.</b> A project holds a show's deep scan,
    track names, colors and options in one file. Changing shows no longer means
    swapping the database and setting everything again.</li>
  <li><b>Open it like any other file.</b> Double-click a project, or use
    File ▸ Open Project… or Open Recent.</li>
  <li><b>Several at once.</b> Each project has its own window. They take turns
    with Pro Tools, and say so when one has to wait.</li>
</ul>
<p>Before you update:</p>
<ul>
  <li><b>You can keep the old database as a backup.</b> It's ticked whenever the
    drive has room. On an exFAT drive it uses as much space as the deep scan, and
    copying a large one takes a while.</li>
  <li><b>Older versions of Assembly can't open projects,</b> so it's best if
    everyone on a show moves together.</li>
  <li><b>Connect the drive with your deep scan first.</b> If it isn't connected,
    Assembly says so and asks again once it's back.</li>
</ul>
<p>Also new:</p>
<ul>
  <li><b>Options save themselves.</b> There's no Save: any option or color you
    change is in the project straight away, and a new project starts from the
    options you used last.</li>
  <li><b>The wrong project is caught.</b> If a session was last used in another
    project, Assembly says so before Match or Align.</li>
  <li><b>A project links to its script</b> and never holds a copy, so passing a
    project on doesn't pass the script with it.</li>
  <li><b>Scan Sound Rolls is now ⇧⌘O.</b> ⌘O is Open Project. Open Database and
    Choose New Database Location have gone: a deep scan lives in its project.</li>
  <li><b>A new project goes in its rolls folder</b> unless you choose
    somewhere else, so it travels with the rolls.</li>
  <li><b>The probes in the Diagnostics menu are out of the way.</b> Open the
    menu and hold Option to see them.</li>
</ul>
<p>Help has a new page, Moving to Projects, with all of this in more detail.</p>
]]></description>
