        <item>
            <title>0.6.9</title>
            <pubDate>Fri, 06 Nov 2026 17:58:42 -0500</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>58</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.6.9</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description><![CDATA[<h2>Assembly 0.6.9</h2>
<p>The toolbar:</p>
<ul>
  <li><b>Every button now has its name under it:</b> Match, Align, Scene/Shot,
    Diagnostic and Help. Match and Scene/Shot are new, and drop down with their
    commands.</li>
  <li><b>Connecting to Pro Tools has moved.</b> Connect and Disconnect are in
    the Match button now, and step 2 always says whether Assembly is connected,
    even before a scan.</li>
</ul>
<p>Assembling:</p>
<ul>
  <li><b>Tracks can go in a folder.</b> A new option in the Tracks card puts an
    assembly's tracks in a folder track named for your prefix, such as
    <code>ASM Assembly</code>. It is off until you turn it on.</li>
  <li><b>Stop finishes the step it is on, then stops.</b> It used to report a
    connection failure at that step.</li>
  <li><b>The custom track color no longer comes up empty.</b> If Pro Tools does
    not give Assembly its palette, the picker now says so and tries again each
    time it opens.</li>
</ul>
<p>Aligning:</p>
<ul>
  <li><b>The progress window says Aligning</b> rather than Assembling.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
