        <item>
            <title>0.6.8</title>
            <pubDate>Fri, 06 Nov 2026 10:45:09 -0500</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>56</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.6.8</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description><![CDATA[<h2>Assembly 0.6.8</h2>
<p>Picture tracks:</p>
<ul>
  <li><b>Scene numbers with a letter inside them now read.</b> Slates like
    <code>2A7-4</code> and <code>V2X38H-1</code> were missed, which left holes
    on the Scene track. Scripts that number scenes this way read too.</li>
  <li><b>A 2 pop is no longer read as a scene.</b> <code>2 POP</code> made a
    one-frame scene 2 at the tail.</li>
  <li><b>A warning when a script hardly fits the cut.</b> Assembly remembers
    the script for later reels, so the last show's can still be loaded. The
    review now warns if it names almost none of the cut's scenes. <b>Clear</b>
    removes it.</li>
</ul>
<p>Aligning lavs to the boom:</p>
<ul>
  <li><b>The report track no longer marks flipped polarity.</b> Turning a lav
    over to match its boom is routine, and one marked its whole take. The
    diagnostic report counts them instead.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
